  "description": "Gardner's minichess played in rounds, as in gardner in rounds, with one change: a collision of two pieces that each capture the other, which in gardner in rounds removes both, goes to whoever holds the initiative. Black holds it at the start. The holder's piece stands on the square, the other is removed, and the initiative passes to the other player, so it decides one meeting at a time and changes hands every time it is used. Two kings stepping onto the same square is no longer a draw: the holder's king takes the other.",
